--- !u!114 &1043496308
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1043496302}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2e86b429b75eb344ba597e172a090920, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  objects:
  - clickableImage: {fileID: 1043496306}
    comments:
    - The past is like a tree's roots. You don't always see them, but they keep us
      standing.
    - History is not just in books. It's in the way we live, the food we eat, even
      the songs we sing.
    - "The heroes you see in paintings\u2026 they were once ordinary people, too.
      But they chose courage."
    - Life in the province is slow, but slow living lets you see what really matters.
    - Every grain of rice you eat has a story. Respect it, for it came from hard
      work.
    - Do not rush to grow up. Time already moves faster than we notice.
    - Books are patient teachers. Even if you close them, they wait for you to return.
    - The window you stare at? It shows the world changing, but also staying the
      same.
    - Heroes are not only those in paintings. Sometimes, heroes are mothers and fathers
      who work for their families.
    - The clock may tick fast in the city, but here in the province, it follows the
      heart's pace.
    - "Ah, these walls\u2026 they have heard prayers, laughter, and even tears. That
      is why the house feels alive."
    - Food is more than flavor. Each dish is memory, passed from one hand to another,
      one generation to the next.
    - Do not underestimate silence. It teaches lessons that noise cannot.
    - "He who does not look back at where he came from\u2026will always get lost
      going forward."
    - "The Philippine flag\u2026 when raised upside down, it means war. That's how
      important its position is."
    - Rizal wrote Noli Me Tangere in Europe, far from home, but every page carried
      his love for the Philippines.
    - When you drink kapeng barako, remember, it comes from Batangas. Strong coffee
      for strong hearts.
    - Our ancestors played larong Pinoy not only for fun, but to teach teamwork and
      discipline.
    - Every weaving pattern in a mat or cloth has meaning. Some patterns are for
      protection, others for blessings.
    - Lapu-Lapu's victory was not just about weapons. It was about pride, the will
      to say 'this land is ours.'
    lastIndex: 0
  popupContainer: {fileID: 167975031}
  popupText: {fileID: 1238174740}
  displayDuration: 4
