--- !u!114 &1447220472
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1447220465}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2e86b429b75eb344ba597e172a090920, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  objects:
  - clickableImage: {fileID: 1447220467}
    comments:
    - "Lola always knows what to say\u2026 even if I don't get it right away."
    - "She's been through so much\u2026 it's kinda inspiring."
    - "Her stories sound like they're straight out of a history book\u2026 but with
      more heart."
    - Sometimes she talks about the past like it happened yesterday.
    - Her food? Legendary. No contest.
    - When Lola laughs, the whole house feels lighter.
    - "Feels weird being back here\u2026 but good weird."
    - The city feels so far away right now.
    - I wonder if this is what people mean by slowing down.
    - "So many memories hiding in this house\u2026 some mine, some way older."
    - The air's different here. Softer, maybe?
    - Funny how being here makes me think about who I really am.
    - Nothing beats a hot kapeng barako in the morning.
    - This cup feels like a warm hug from Lola.
    - Simple, strong, no fancy cafe needed.
    - "Steam rising, crickets chirping outside\u2026 this is peak probinsya vibes."
    - Kinda bitter, but in a good way.
    - All I hear are birds, leaves, and maybe a tricycle far away.
    - The sky looks bigger out here.
    - "It smells like soil after rain\u2026 fresh."
    - "So many stars at night\u2026 can't see that in the city."
    - The neighbors actually say hi here. Weird, but nice.
    - "Simple but tough\u2026 like it's seen decades of muddy slippers."
    - I remember wiping my feet here as a kid.
    - Looks handmade. Bet it has its own little history.
    - Feels like part of the house's personality.
    - Kinda funny seeing lechon and adobo painted like art.
    - Cool how they mix games and food in the same wall.
    - These paintings aren't just pretty, they're like little culture lessons.
    - Every brush stroke feels like it's telling a story I half-remember.
    - It's history, but with colors and flavors.
    - The view from here is like a painting that keeps moving.
    - When the breeze comes through, it feels like the house is breathing.
    - I used to peek out here as a kid, waiting for ice cream carts.
    - "This window frames the world outside\u2026 makes it look calmer."
    - I can hear kids playing just by leaning closer.
    - Sunlight pouring in makes the whole room glow.
    - It's like the window keeps secrets, what it's seen over the years.
    - Lola, why does your food taste better than five-star restaurants? Oh right,
      it's free.
    - 'Deep thought of the day: am I hungry, or just bored?'
    - If mosquitoes had a leaderboard, I'd be number one target.
    - One sip and I'm awake. Two sips and I'm questioning my life choices.
    - If I drink three cups, will I see the future?
    - Why does coffee here taste like wisdom and regrets?
    - "Is that a carabao\u2026 or just a very buff cow?"
    - The air's so fresh, I almost feel guilty breathing too much of it.
    - Every insect outside thinks I'm a buffet.
    - Step here, and suddenly you're a good houseguest.
    - I think this mat deserves a vacation too.
    - Imagine being a mat. Everyone steps on you, but you never complain.
    - Why do the food paintings look like they're judging my diet?
    - This window has better resolution than my phone screen.
    - "Standing here makes me look deep and mysterious\u2026 until I sneeze."
    lastIndex: 0
  popupContainer: {fileID: 263593513}
  popupText: {fileID: 18283869}
  displayDuration: 4
